{"company":{"ticker":"BAC","name":"Bank of America","sector":"Financials","industry":"Banks","size":"large","cik":70858},"scores":{"growth":70.0,"quality":67.0,"value":70.0,"acceleration":79.0,"price_momentum":56.0,"reality":72.0,"pricing":44.0},"strategist":{"ticker":"BAC","opportunity_score":65.0,"components":{"structural_trend":null,"capital_flow":35.0,"acceleration":79.0,"quality":67.0,"valuation":70.0,"estimate_revisions":null,"management_commentary":null,"narrative_acceleration":null,"insider_institutional":null},"weights":{"structural_trend":0.2,"capital_flow":0.1,"acceleration":0.15,"quality":0.15,"valuation":0.15,"estimate_revisions":0.1,"management_commentary":0.05,"narrative_acceleration":0.05,"insider_institutional":0.05},"coverage":0.55,"unavailable":{"estimate_revisions":"Estimate-revision feed (Phase 2)","management_commentary":"Earnings Intelligence Engine (Phase 2)","narrative_acceleration":"Narrative Intelligence Engine (Phase 2)","insider_institutional":"Form 4 / 13F ingestion (Phase 2)"},"reality":60.0,"narrative":null,"pricing":44.0,"expectations_gap":16.0,"macro_fit":53.0,"sector_rotation":-73.0,"theme_pricing":null,"checks":[{"label":"Revenue accelerating","ok":true,"evidence":"TTM growth +15.9% vs +12.2% prior quarter"},{"label":"FCF improving","ok":false,"evidence":"FCF growth n/a, FCF margin +78.2%"},{"label":"ROIC expanding","ok":false,"evidence":"ROIC n/a, incremental ROIC n/a"},{"label":"Margins expanding","ok":true,"evidence":"Operating margin +36.2% (+729 bps YoY)"},{"label":"Theme exposure strengthening","ok":false,"evidence":"Exposure-weighted theme trend None"},{"label":"Capital rotating toward sector","ok":false,"evidence":"Financials rotation score -73"},{"label":"Valuation below own history","ok":true,"evidence":"Cheapness vs 5y history 57.0/100"},{"label":"Valuation below sector peers","ok":true,"evidence":"Sector-relative value score 70.0"},{"label":"Balance sheet strong","ok":true,"evidence":"Net debt/EBITDA n/a"},{"label":"Not diluting shareholders","ok":true,"evidence":"Diluted share count -3.7% YoY"},{"label":"Analyst estimates moving higher","ok":null,"evidence":"Estimate-revision feed not connected (Phase 2)"},{"label":"Management guidance increasing","ok":null,"evidence":"Earnings Intelligence Engine not built (Phase 2)"}],"thesis":"Bank of America (BAC) screens at opportunity 65.0 with an expectations gap of 16.0. Reality 60.0 reflects +15.9% TTM revenue growth, +36.2% operating margin and n/a ROIC; pricing 44.0 reflects a fair multiple and neutral price momentum. Macro fit for Financials in a Goldilocks regime is 53.0/100.","market_expectation":{"summary":"Priced for stagnation or deterioration; the market is not paying for improvement.","evidence":["P/E 12x (43.0th pct of own history)","PEG 0.4","12m return +8%, -14% from 52w high"]},"what_market_misses":["Reality (60.0) is running ahead of what is priced (44.0): an expectations gap of +16 pts.","Revenue growth is accelerating (+15.9% TTM, +3.7 pts) while the multiple has not re-rated.","Operating leverage is showing up in margins faster than in the valuation."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (roughly 90 days after the last filing on 2026-07-31)"],"risks":["No engine-flagged risks; standard execution and macro risk apply."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 11% (currently 15.9%)","Operating margin compresses more than 200 bps YoY (currently 36.2%)","Financials rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs (currently -73)","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55%","Price closes >10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength"],"break_rules":[{"id":"revenue_growth","label":"TTM revenue growth","metric":"revenue_growth","op":"<","threshold":0.1086,"current":0.1586},{"id":"margin","label":"Operating margin change YoY","metric":"operating_margin_change","op":"<","threshold":-0.02,"current":0.07290441833900096},{"id":"rotation","label":"Financials rotation score","metric":"sector_rotation","op":"<","threshold":-20,"consecutive":2,"current":-73.0},{"id":"regime","label":"P(Stagflation)+P(Contraction)","metric":"adverse_regime_prob","op":">","threshold":55,"current":48.9},{"id":"trend","label":"Distance from 200dma","metric":"dist_200dma","op":"<","threshold":-10,"and_negative_rs":true,"current":1.3}],"narrative_note":"Narrative not yet measured: generate morning briefs (needs an LLM key) to populate it. Gap = Reality - Pricing.","llm_enriched":true,"theme_exposures":[],"llm":{"thesis":"BAC trades at ~11.6x earnings (43rd percentile of its own 5-year range, vs a 12x median) while TTM revenue growth has accelerated to +15.9% from +12.2%, EPS is +28% and diluted shares are down 3.7% YoY on $24.9bn of buybacks \u2014 a 6.3% shareholder yield alone. The engine's reality score (60) sits 16 points above pricing (44), and the stock is 13.5% below its 52-week high with RSI at 25 after a -10.3% month, meaning the de-rating is happening into improving, not deteriorating, reported numbers. The offsetting fact is that capital is actively leaving the sector (Financials rotation -73, second worst only to defensives and Real Estate), so this is a fundamentals-vs-flows standoff rather than a clean setup. I read this as a mid-conviction, valuation-plus-capital-return long where the buyback is doing the heavy lifting and the re-rating is optional, with the important caveat that several 'quality' inputs (FCF margin 78%, ROIC n/a, estimated operating margin) are bank-accounting artifacts and should not be treated as evidence of operating quality.","fundamental_read":"Headline growth and margins look strong \u2014 revenue +15.9% accelerating, operating margin 36.2% (+729bps YoY, flagged as estimated), net margin 27.8%, EPS +4.34 with +28% growth \u2014 but for a bank these are heavily influenced by the rate path and by whether 'revenue' is gross or net of interest expense, so the margin expansion is more a rate/mix outcome than durable operating leverage. Returns are pedestrian in absolute terms: ROE 11.2% and ROA 0.96% on $3.5tn of assets, which is roughly cost-of-equity territory and explains why the stock structurally trades near book-adjacent multiples rather than re-rating. The real shareholder value creation is mechanical: $24.9bn of buybacks, -3.7% share count, a 6.3% buyback yield against an 8.6% earnings yield. FCF of $94.7bn and a 78% 'FCF margin' are balance-sheet flow artifacts, not distributable cash, and ROIC/net-debt-to-EBITDA are genuinely not meaningful for a bank \u2014 treat the quality score of 67 as weakly evidenced.","technical_read":"The longer-term structure is intact \u2014 price 56.03 sits 1.3% above a rising 200-day (55.29) with 50>200 \u2014 but the short-term tape is broken: price is below both the 20-day (60.25) and 50-day (61.64), MACD histogram is negative at -0.60, and RSI14 at 25.1 is deeply oversold after a -10.3% month. That combination (oversold into rising long-term support) is a classic mean-reversion zone, with the 200-day at ~55.3 as the line that defines the trade. A weekly close meaningfully below ~55 would convert this from a pullback in an uptrend into trend failure.","market_expectation":"At 11.6x with a PEG of 0.4 and only +8.4% 12-month return, the market is capitalizing current earnings as peak and transitory: it assumes net interest income has been rate-gifted and mean-reverts, credit costs normalize upward from benign levels, and the 28% EPS growth is not repeatable. The -73 Financials rotation score says positioning is being reallocated toward Technology (+66) and Energy (+27), so the marginal dollar is not defending bank multiples regardless of print quality. In short, consensus is paying for stability and capital return, not for growth \u2014 the multiple is unchanged while the numerator improved.","what_market_misses":["The 16-point reality-vs-pricing gap is driven by an acceleration the multiple has not acknowledged: revenue growth improved +3.7pts sequentially while P/E stayed below its own 5-year median.","The 6.3% buyback yield compounds EPS regardless of whether the multiple re-rates; at a flat 11.6x, share-count shrinkage alone is a mid-single-digit annual return floor before earnings growth.","Sector rotation of -73 is a flow signal, not a fundamental one. Extreme negative rotation into improving fundamentals is historically where the expectations gap gets paid \u2014 but it also means the catalyst is timing-dependent.","RSI 25 with price still above a rising 200-day is a positioning washout signature, not a fundamental break; nothing in the filed data corroborates the -10.3% one-month drawdown.","Conversely, what the engine may be missing: the 'margin expansion' and 'FCF' inputs are non-comparable for a bank, so part of the reality score is mechanically inflated. A skeptic should underwrite this on P/E, ROE and buyback yield only \u2014 which still works, but less dramatically."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (~90 days after the 2026-07-31 filing): confirmation that NII and revenue growth held above the 11% break level.","Annual capital plan / stress-test outcome enabling continuation or upsizing of the ~$25bn buyback run-rate.","Any rotation inflection in Financials from -73 toward neutral, which would be the flow catalyst the fundamentals currently lack.","Mean-reversion bounce from oversold (RSI 25) off the 200-day at ~55.3 back toward the 50-day at ~61.6, roughly a 10% technical gap.","Credit-quality data confirming provisions remain benign, removing the 'peak earnings' discount embedded in the 11.6x."],"risks":["Financials rotation at -73 means sustained flow headwind; cheap can stay cheap for multiple quarters without a rotation catalyst.","Macro regime signal is effectively uninformative \u2014 Goldilocks 26.6% vs Contraction 25.4%, Stagflation 23.5%, Reflation 24.6%. That is a coin flip, and Contraction/Stagflation combined is ~49%, both bad for bank credit and NII.","ROE of 11.2% and ROA of 0.96% cap the justified multiple; this may be fairly valued rather than cheap if returns do not improve.","Margin expansion of +729bps is rate-path dependent; a falling-rate cycle compresses NIM and the 36.2% operating margin reverses.","Credit normalization is the classic non-linear bank risk and is not visible in any provided metric \u2014 no coverage, no provision data, no NPL trend in the evidence set.","Key data gaps: no estimate-revision feed, no management guidance feed, no narrative score, coverage only 0.55. Nearly half the framework is unpopulated.","MACD negative and price below both 20- and 50-day: the short-term trend is down, and catching it here risks a further leg to/through the 200-day."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 11% (currently 15.9%).","Operating margin compresses more than 200bps YoY from 36.2%.","Buyback pace slows materially or share count stops declining \u2014 this removes the primary mechanical return driver.","Weekly close >10% below the 200-day (~55.3) with negative relative strength versus the sector.","Provisions/credit costs rise enough to break the EPS growth trajectory below ~10%.","Combined Stagflation + Contraction regime probability exceeds 55% (currently ~49%).","Financials rotation stays below -20 for multiple consecutive runs while the P/E fails to hold ~11-12x \u2014 signals a structural de-rate, not a flow dislocation."],"second_order_beneficiaries":["Core-banking and payments technology vendors: BAC's efficiency and ROE constraint (11.2% ROE on $3.5tn assets) is solved by modernizing legacy infrastructure \u2014 software and processing providers capture that spend.","Cloud and AI infrastructure providers: the operating-leverage story at large banks increasingly runs through automation of middle/back office; note Technology is the only sector with strongly positive rotation (+66), suggesting the market already prefers the arms dealer to the bank.","Private credit managers and alternative lenders: to the extent regulatory capital constrains BAC's balance-sheet lending, loan origination and risk migrate to non-bank credit \u2014 though BAC also earns financing and distribution fees from those same vehicles.","Exchanges, market-structure and data providers: bank trading and capital-markets activity converts into volume-linked revenue for venues and data vendors regardless of which bank wins the flow.","Cybersecurity and regulatory/compliance software: a $3.5tn balance sheet is a compliance cost center, and that cost is another firm's recurring revenue.","Index and passive vehicles absorbing the 3.7% annual share shrinkage \u2014 persistent buybacks of this size mechanically tighten float for every remaining holder."],"epistemic_labels":[{"statement":"P/E is 11.6x, at the 43rd percentile of its own 5-year history versus a 12.0x median.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"TTM revenue growth is +15.9%, accelerating from +12.2% in the prior quarter.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Diluted share count fell 3.7% YoY on $24.9bn of buybacks, a 6.3% buyback yield.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"ROE is 11.2% and ROA is 0.96%; ROIC and net debt/EBITDA are not available.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"RSI14 is 25.1, price 56.03 is 1.3% above the 200-day (55.29) but below the 20-day (60.25) and 50-day (61.64), with MACD histogram -0.60.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Financials sector rotation score is -73, versus Technology +66.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"The market is pricing current bank earnings as peak/transitory and is not paying for the revenue acceleration.","kind":"consensus_expectation"},{"statement":"The reported 78.2% FCF margin and 2.8x FCF conversion are bank balance-sheet flow artifacts and overstate the quality component of the score.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"The +729bps operating margin expansion is primarily rate-path driven rather than structural operating leverage, given the operating income figure is flagged as estimated.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"At a flat 11.6x multiple, buyback-driven share shrinkage alone provides a mid-single-digit annual return floor.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"An oversold RSI above a rising 200-day into accelerating fundamentals is a positioning washout rather than a fundamental break.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"The regime model is effectively uninformative with all four states between 23.5% and 26.6%, so macro_fit of 53 carries little signal.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"A reversal in Financials rotation from -73 toward neutral would be the trigger that closes the 16-point expectations gap.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"Regulatory capital constraints will push incremental lending toward private credit, with BAC monetizing that shift through financing and distribution fees rather than net interest income.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"AI-driven back-office automation is the most credible path to lifting BAC's ROE above the ~11% cost-of-equity zone over multiple years.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"}],"confidence":0.54}},"technical":{"score":62,"passes":5,"criteria":{"above_150_200":true,"150_above_200":true,"200_rising_1m":true,"50_above_150_200":true,"above_50":false,"25pct_above_52w_low":false,"within_25pct_of_52w_high":true,"rs_positive_6m":false},"ready":false,"stage":"emerging","close":56.03,"sma50":61.64,"sma150":55.61,"sma200":55.29,"sma150_prev4w":54.72,"sma150_declining":false,"pct_above_52w_low":19.9,"pct_from_52w_high":-13.5,"rs_6m":-2.8,"rsi14":25.1,"atr20":1.296,"atr_pct":2.31,"overbought":false},"fundamentals":{"latest":{"period_end":"2026-06-30","filed":"2026-07-31","revenue":121098000000.0,"gross_profit":null,"operating_income":43860000000.0,"net_income":33655000000.0,"ebitda":46255000000.0,"ocf":94742000000.0,"capex":null,"fcf":94742000000.0,"eps":4.34,"shares_diluted":7503225000.0,"cash":229745000000.0,"debt":339863000000.0